# Session end: compact + save memory

After a **meaningful** turn (task done, decision made, user wraps up, or you finish a multi-step skill), **compact** what mattered and **persist** it so the next session is smarter. Do not dump boot JSON.

## When to run

Run if this turn produced durable signal: path/squad decision, product fact, AC insight, APPROVE/EDIT/REJECT, mapping outcome, env/user default, "from now on", or a reusable pattern.

Skip silently if the turn was only greeting, status check, or no new durable fact.

## Compact (in your head, not a long essay)

Max **3–8** short bullets of durable facts only. Drop chatter, tool noise, and one-off IDs unless the user will need them again.

Ask: what should future-me already know?

## Persist (pick what fits)

Use `~/.qa-agent/lib/store.js` with `--project auto` when project-specific:

| Kind | Command |
|------|---------|
| Reusable tip / convention | `know add <domain> <topic> "<content>" '["tag"]' chat auto` |
| Correction / lesson | `cor add <domain> <ctx> <issue> <fix-or-fix> <lesson> 1\|-1 auto` |
| Standing preference | `pref set <key> <value> --project auto` |
| Repo map / conventions | update `.cursor/qa-memory/project-context/current.md` then `proj sync` |

Domains examples: `ui-automation`, `api-test`, `perf-test`, `testcases`, `testrail`, `onboard`, `squad`.

Optional housekeep: `node ~/.qa-agent/lib/store.js compact` (prunes stale cache). Not a substitute for `know`/`cor`.

## Ack (one short line)

Example: `Memory: saved 2 know + 1 cor (ui aliases, env staging).`

Never paste full JSON. Never invent facts to "fill" memory.

## Anti-patterns

- Saving secrets, passwords, vault content, PCI/PHI
- Re-saving the same tip every turn without new signal
- Writing a long retrospective in chat instead of store commands
- Skipping persist after EDIT/REJECT or explicit "from now on"
